From 55510c261e6b8f0b53d7d679c9934e52129ec900 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:55:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): register containment SQL functions once per
 connection [daveey]

SQLite refuses replacement of a user function while any statement is active. Keep a connection-owned callable and refresh its Python callback, preserving verifier and snapshot behavior without replacing the SQL registration. Weak-value bookkeeping is released on connection close; plain SQLite connections need no weakref support. Quarantine modules have no create_function sites.

Proof: active-cursor RED 6 failed/1 passed; GREEN 9 passed including stop+release certify_page and close cleanup. scripts/check --base origin/main passed.
